## opensift deploying apps

# find console url from cli
oc whoami --show-console
- os uses external identity providers (kube:admin defalut, should be removed after admin pwd change)

# perspective
- administrator (administration of individual resources, not admin priviledges!)/developer (focus on app deployment) switch on top left

creating a project
- project is an os extension of kubernetes namespace project (adds RBAC)
- in project pane you have tiles to create items...

create a deployment
- form, select image, resource type, advanced options...
- shows as an app

admin view
- project actions for deployment: enable health checks
- adding environment vars 
- events -- sort of logs 
- when you modify the pod template in deployment -- pods get recated 

- pod details -- similar to deployment view, if you delete the pod, it gets recreated if deployment has replicaset defined
- logs: container sourced log
- terminal: get into the container, good for troubleshooting
- env tab -- read only in the pod view

- for all resources you can modify yaml same as in cli
- route/secure route -- the latter is with https

# deployment from a source code
- builder images -- contains dependencies for various languages 
- dev perspective - add - deploy from git - edit builder strategy to detect lang environment if needed
- *build resource* - controls the runtime env and the build, pulls the builder image, builds it and builds application image on top of it, pushes it to the internal openshift registry
- add a webhook - redeploy on git change, in git repo -- add webhook, payload url (os instance)

- the same form cli:
oc new-app --name pyweb <git-project-url> # but a problem if os cant detect lang
- imagestream -- internal representation of a repository in os
oc new-app --name pyweb python:3.8-ubi8~<git-project-url> # syntax: `builder image to deploy on + ~ + git url` 
oc get pods # app created

# Developer catalog 
- pre-installed backi builders in os: 
- templates -- combination of reasources, can be parametrized
- devFiles -- ci/cd decriptions
- * helmCharts -- versioned resource combinations, like templates but with history 


## opensift-odo

cli tool for deployment/development (optional utility for os)
- description of CI/CD pipeline
- supports various langs

- go to project dir
odo init
- detects lang version, runs cli questionare
- creates files: dev file (covers deployment and development parts -- in the second you define commands you want to run), dockerfile, kubernetes resources (all are templates)

odo dev --platform podman
-- creates a container locally, and inside it runs the application
-- it watches the directory, it redeploys on source code change

odo login -u developer -p developer
-- configure odo to use openshift

odo create namespace <myspace>
odo deploy
-- reads the spec from the dev file and builds the image, pushes it, creates the resources
